  "sourceData": {
    "answer": "to: blink-(one's-eyes)/wink/bat | twinkle-(e.g.-stars)/flicker/waver",
    "mnemonic": "Because the hiragana ends with an <ja>う</ja> sound, you know this word is a verb. The kanji itself means <kanji>blink</kanji> and the verb vocab version is <vocabulary>to blink</vocabulary>.\n\nThis word is generally used in the phrase 瞬く間に (in the blink of an eye).",
    "readingMnemonic": "<reading>Mah ta ta</reading> (<ja>またた</ja>) is showing, causing you <vocabulary>to blink</vocabulary>. I don't know what a \"tata\" is, but I bet you could come up with something that's blink-worthy."
